Q: iOS keyboard breaks page layout when opened A: <p>You are only updating the visual viewports height. On IOS, opening the keyboard can also change <code>visualViewport.offsetTop</code>, which leaves the container positioned partly outside the visible area.</p>
<p>Update both values and use them to position the fixed outer container. Also prevent the document itself from scrolling so only the message container scrolls.</p>
<p><strong>CSS</strong></p>
<pre><code>html, body, #root {
  height: 100%;
  margin: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.app {
  position: fixed;
  top: var(--app-top, 0px);
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  height: var(--app-height, 100dvh);
}

.message-container {
  min-height: 0;
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>React</strong></p>
<pre><code>componentDidMount() {
   this.viewport = window.visualViewport;
   this.updateViewport();

   (this.viewport || window).addEventListener('resize', this.updateViewport);
   this.viewport?.addEventListener('scroll', this.updateViewport);
}

componentWillUnmount() {
   (this.viewport || window).removeEventListener('resize', this.updateViewport);
   this.viewport?.removeEventListener('scroll', this.updateViewport);
}

updateViewport = () =&gt; {
   const viewport = this.viewport;
   const style = document.documentElement.style;

   style.setProperty(
       '--app-height',
       `${viewport?.height ?? window.innerHeight}px`
   );

   style.setProperty(
       '--app-top',
       `${viewport?.offsetTop ?? 0}px`
   );
};

render() {
   return (
       &lt;div className=&quot;app container-fluid d-flex flex-column p-0&quot;&gt;
           &lt;div
               ref={this.messagesContainerRef}
               className=&quot;message-container d-flex flex-column flex-grow-1 overflow-auto p-3&quot;
           &gt;
               {this.renderMessages(this.state.messages)}
           &lt;/div&gt;

           &lt;form
               className=&quot;border-top border-light bg-body flex-shrink-0 p-2&quot;
               onSubmit={e =&gt; {
                   e.preventDefault();
                   this.checkAndSend();
               }}
           &gt;
               &lt;div className=&quot;input-group&quot;&gt;
                   ...
               &lt;/div&gt;
           &lt;/form&gt;
       &lt;/div&gt;
   );
}
</code></pre>

Q: Hover over an item in the dropdown list in selenium webdriver A: <p>Check this example how we could implement this.</p>

<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/OELUN.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/OELUN.png" alt="enter image description here"></a></p>

<pre><code>public class HoverableDropdownTest {

    private WebDriver driver;
    private Actions action;

    Consumer &lt; By &gt; hover = (By by) - &gt; {
        action.moveToElement(driver.findElement(by))
              .perform();
    };

    @Test
    public void hoverTest() {
        driver.get("https://www.bootply.com/render/6FC76YQ4Nh");

        hover.accept(By.linkText("Dropdown"));
        hover.accept(By.linkText("Dropdown Link 5"));
        hover.accept(By.linkText("Dropdown Submenu Link 5.4"));
        hover.accept(By.linkText("Dropdown Submenu Link 5.4.1"));
    }

    @BeforeTest
    public void setupDriver() {
        driver = new FirefoxDriver();
        action = new Actions(driver);
    }

    @AfterTest
    public void teardownDriver() {
        driver.quit();
    }

}
</code></pre>

<p>For detailed answer, check here - <a href="http://www.testautomationguru.com/selenium-webdriver-automating-hoverable-multilevel-dropdowns/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">http://www.testautomationguru.com/selenium-webdriver-automating-hoverable-multilevel-dropdowns/</a></p>

Q: How to read multiple sets of value in the excel sheet using DataProvider in Selenium WebDriver with Java and TestNG A: <p>Dependencies used:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.poi&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;poi&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;3.13&lt;/version&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;

&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.poi&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;poi-ooxml&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;3.13&lt;/version&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;

&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.testng&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;testng&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;6.14.3&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Code goes here to read xlsx file:</p>

<pre><code>import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;

import org.apache.poi.openxml4j.exceptions.InvalidFormatException;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.DataFormatter;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.usermodel.XSSFCell;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.usermodel.XSSFRow;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.usermodel.XSSFSheet;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.usermodel.XSSFWorkbook;
import org.testng.annotations.DataProvider;
import org.testng.annotations.Test;

public class TestDataProvider {
    static File resultFile = new File(“PATH OF THE EXCEL”);
    public static DataFormatter formatter = new DataFormatter();

    @Test(dataProvider = "readExcelFile")
    public static void test1(String slNum, String name, String Address, String email) throws  IOException {
        System.out.println(slNum+" "+ name+" "+Address + " "+email);

    FURTHER CODE GOES HERE


    }

    @DataProvider
    public static Object[][] readExcelFile() throws InvalidFormatException, IOException {
        FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(resultFile);
        XSSFWorkbook wb = new XSSFWorkbook(fis);
        XSSFSheet sh = wb.getSheet(“SHEET NAME”);

        System.out.println(sh.getPhysicalNumberOfRows());
        System.out.println(sh.getRow(0).getPhysicalNumberOfCells());
        int RowNum = sh.getPhysicalNumberOfRows();
        int ColNum = sh.getRow(0).getPhysicalNumberOfCells();

        String[][] xlData = new String[RowNum-1][ColNum];

        for (int i = 0; i &lt; RowNum - 1; i++) 
        {
            XSSFRow row = sh.getRow(i + 1);
            for (int j = 0; j &lt; ColNum; j++) 
            {
                if (row == null)
                    xlData[i][j] = "";
                else {
                    XSSFCell cell = row.getCell(j);                 
                    if (cell == null)
                        xlData[i][j] = ""; 
                    else {
                        String value = formatter.formatCellValue(cell);
                        xlData[i][j] = value.trim();                        
                    }
                }
            }
        }       
        return xlData;
    }   
}
</code></pre>

Q: Find a specific string in an Excel file using Apache POI API A: <p>There are two bugs I noticed in your code. First, you write the file every time you remove a row which is inefficient. Second, you only search the FIRST string-cell in the row, and if the first string-cell in the row isn't the correct one, you break.  If your automatically generated file saves numbers or blank cells as strings (possible), then this will cause a difference between your hand generated excel file and the one you created with the script. I would suggest removing the second break statement. To clean up the code, I would rewrite the whole if block as follows:</p>

<pre><code>if(cell.getCellType() == Cell.CELL_TYPE_STRING &amp;&amp; cell.getStringCellValue().equals("GET")){
    sheet.removeRow(row);
    break;
} else {
    System.out.print("Not Found! ");
}
</code></pre>

<p>The if statement works because of short circuiting. This will save you a whole lot of time if you are new to apache poi. :)</p>

<p>After we have removed the rows, we should then write the file.
Place the following after the whole for block:</p>

<pre><code>try (FileOutputStream fileOut = new FileOutputStream("C:/juni.xls")) {
    wb.write(fileOut);
}
</code></pre>

<p>I'm assuming that sheet.removeRow(row) will work in an enhanced for loop. If it doesn't, you may need to fix it or make your code work in a while loop. Hint:  while((row = sheet.getRow(i)) != null ){  }</p>

Q: Horizontal Slider X axis A: <p>You can determine which slide is currently in view by comparing each slide's horizontal bounds (getBoundingClientRect().left) against the slider container's visible bounds during the scroll (or wheel) event.</p>
<p>Here is a straightforward approach:</p>
<pre><code>const scrollContainer = document.querySelector('.slider');
const slides = document.querySelectorAll('.slide');

const activeSlide = () =&gt; {
    const containerRect = scrollContainer.getBoundingClientRect();

    slides.forEach( (element) =&gt; {
        const slideRect = element.getBoundingClientRect();

        // Check if the center of the slide (element) is inside the container's visible area
        const slideCenter = slideRect.left + slideRect.width / 2;

        if( slideCenter &gt;= containerRect.left &amp;&amp; slideCenter &lt;= containerRect.right ) {

            console.log('Current visible slide:', element);
        }
    });
};

scrollContainer.addEventListener( 'wheel', (event) =&gt; {
    event.preventDefault();
    scrollContainer.scrollLeft += event.deltaY;

    activeSlide();
});
</code></pre>
<p>How it works:</p>
<p>slideRect.left + slideRect.width / 2 finds the exact horizontal center of each slide.</p>
<p>It checks if that center point falls between the left and right boundaries of your .slider container.</p>
